/STR f5670047
To whom?
/STR e079e0f2
You already gave her all you had.
/STR 78ab7830
The reals are in the saddlebags. Take them out first.
/STR 92753a5a
You have nothing to give. (Didn't you keep something for a rainy day, at home?)
/STR da52ca1c
Durandarte lies on his marble tomb, his right hand on the side of his heart, which he no longer has.
/STR 662cf649
A venerable old man, in a hooded cloak of purple baize, with a white beard that reaches below his waist.
/STR 49ea7ff8
It is the same country girl from El Toboso. Dulcinea, enchanted, skipping across the meadow.
/STR 3a874896
Montesinos looks at you as if waiting for you to speak to him. It would be discourteous to leave like this.
/STR 5d9cf4be
You don't walk out of the crystal palace. At most, you wait for them to pull on the rope.
/STR 18a82ff5
The cousin won't let you go without going down the cave: that's what he came for, and so did you.
/STR 4211352b
