A grave ecclesiastic, one of those who, not being born princes, never manage to teach those who are how to be so.
/STR 4e839bc3
The dukes, who have read Part One of your history and are having a wonderful time.
/STR ea158060
A countess in mourning, with a train in three points and a beard the barber of your village would envy.
/STR 74519d85
A wooden horse, with a peg in its forehead. They say that if you turn it, it flies. They say so.
/STR cc3139b0
The Distressed Duenna stops you: {i6}"Blindfolded, sir knight, for otherwise the height will make you giddy."{i7}
